{"type":"step-done","workflow":"build","step":"build-challenge","status":"DONE","at":"2026-11-08T21:08:14Z","parentSha":"fc51e356cca32700ecd979fc927fd90e37898100","artifacts":["docs/plans/202611/logs/892-template-copies-bkit/build-challenge-1.md","docs/plans/202611/logs/892-template-copies-bkit/build-challenge-2.md"],"verdict":"CONCERNS","attempt":1,"failures":0,"round":1,"challengeFindings":[{"severity":"MEDIUM","location":".bkit/core/engine/install/template-copies.ts:81","title":"A consumer with lint-staged installed and no root lint-staged config upgrades, the sync deletes `.bkit/templates/.lintstagedrc.json` (the only config lint-staged found), and every later commit fails in pre-commit with \"Configuration could not be found\""},{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/core/engine/audits/templates/template-path-refs.test.ts:61","title":"A workflow or prompt can now name `.prettierignore` or `.lintstagedrc.json` (an adopted-template path) and the template-path guard stays green, because the forbidden names derive from template file names and the rename dropped both destination names"},{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/core/hooks/gateguard-engine.js:18","title":"An agent editing bkit's own `.bkit/templates/prettierignore.example` or `lintstagedrc.example.json` gets the generic checklist instead of the gate-config advisory, because `GATE_CONFIG_PATTERNS` match only the old dotfile basenames, while the hook comment says bkit's template source \"stays guarded\""},{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/core/docs/templates/bkit-audit-adoption.md:116","title":"The adoption audit's reconcile step runs `diff .bkit/templates/<path> <path>`, which for the renamed samples diffs against a root `prettierignore.example` / `lintstagedrc.example.json` that never exists, and its merged check runs `git log` on a path whose history starts at the upgrade commit, so an adopted `.prettierignore` reads as unreconciled or pending"}]}
